IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdba-nouns`
IMPORT `cdba-calendar`

-- Canada Disability Benefit Regulations (SOR/2025-35), sections 32 to 34 -- COMPLIANCE AND
-- ENFORCEMENT: when a person must give the Minister information or documents, or be available.
--
-- Whether a judge grants an authorization (s 32(4)), what a judge does on review (s 32(7)),
-- and the use of certified copies as evidence (s 33) are the Minister's and the court's
-- business, and are inert (NOTES.md, coverage).

§ `Regulations s 32 -- Inspections`

DECLARE `Kind of person asked for information` IS ONE OF
    `an applicant`
    `a beneficiary`
    `the representative of an applicant or beneficiary who is incapable of managing their own affairs`
    `any other person`

-- 32(2) and 32(3): the Minister may require any person to provide information or a document
-- by a notice served personally or by confirmed delivery service, within the reasonable time
-- the notice specifies. For anyone other than an applicant, a beneficiary or such a
-- representative, the Minister needs a judge's authorization first, served with the notice.
-- src:273 | (2) Despite any other provision of the Act or these Regulations, the Minister may, subject to subsection (3), by notice served personally or by confirmed delivery service, require that any person provide any information or document for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of the Act or these Regulations within the reasonable time specified in the notice.
-- src:274 | Other persons
-- src:275 | (3) The Minister must obtain the authorization of a judge under subsection (4) before requiring that a person — other than an applicant, a beneficiary or the representative of an applicant or beneficiary who is incapable of managing their own affairs — provide information or documents under subsection (2).
@ref Regulations s 32(2) and (3) (src:273-275)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of person asked for information`
      `the notice was served personally or by confirmed delivery service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a judge authorized the Minister to require it and the authorization was served together with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is required to provide the information or document` kind `the notice was served personally or by confirmed delivery service` `the notice specifies a reasonable time` `a judge authorized the Minister to require it and the authorization was served together with the notice` MEANS
        `the notice was served personally or by confirmed delivery service`
    AND `the notice specifies a reasonable time`
    AND (CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `an applicant` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a beneficiary` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the representative of an applicant or beneficiary who is incapable of managing their own affairs` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `any other person` THEN `a judge authorized the Minister to require it and the authorization was served together with the notice`)

-- 32(6): the person served with an authorization and a notice may apply to the judge for a
-- review not later than 15 days after the day they are served.
-- src:281 | (6) A person on whom an authorization and a notice are served under subsection (5) may, not later than 15 days after the day on which the authorization and notice are served, apply to the judge who granted the authorization under subsection (4) or, if that judge is unable to act, to another judge of the same court for a review of the authorization.
@ref Regulations s 32(6) (src:281)
GIVEN `the day the authorization and notice were served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply for a review of the authorization` `the day the authorization and notice were served` MEANS
    `the day the authorization and notice were served` PLUS 15

§ `Regulations s 34 -- Obligation to appear`

-- 34: for a purpose related to verifying compliance or preventing non-compliance, the
-- Minister may require an applicant, a beneficiary or such a representative to be at a
-- suitable place, or available by audioconference, videoconference or another suitable
-- manner, at a suitable time, to provide information or a document related to the application.
-- src:289 | 34 The Minister may, for any purpose related to verifying compliance or preventing non-compliance with the Act or these Regulations, require an applicant, a beneficiary or the representative of an applicant or beneficiary who is incapable of managing their own affairs to be at a suitable place — or to be available by audioconference or videoconference or in any other suitable manner — at a suitable time in order to provide any information or document related to their application that the Minister may require.
@ref Regulations s 34 (src:289)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of person asked for information`
      `the Minister requires it for a purpose related to verifying compliance or preventing non-compliance with the Act or these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is required to be at a suitable place or available at a suitable time` kind `the Minister requires it for a purpose related to verifying compliance or preventing non-compliance with the Act or these Regulations` MEANS
        `the Minister requires it for a purpose related to verifying compliance or preventing non-compliance with the Act or these Regulations`
    AND (CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `an applicant` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a beneficiary` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the representative of an applicant or beneficiary who is incapable of managing their own affairs` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `any other person` THEN FALSE)
